        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260415-from-yaound%C3%A9-to-bamenda-cameroonians-await-pope-leo-xiv-s-visit",
        "orario": "17:30",
        "timestamp": 1776267011,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. From Yaoundé to Bamenda, Cameroonians await Pope Leo XIV’s visit Issued on: 15/04/2026 - 17:30 Pope Leo XIV visits Cameroon from April 15th to 18th. During his stay, the pontiff will visit three cities in the country: Yaoundé, the capital; Douala, the economic hub; and Bamenda, the capital of the Northwest region, which has been gripped by a socio-political crisis for a decade. Two days before his arrival, the Christian community of Cameroon is preparing for Leo XIV, who will be the third pontiff to set foot on Cameroonian soil, as FRANCE 24’s team on the ground reports. The school in Kenya where education is empowering teenage mothers 15/04/2026 Sudan enters fourth year of war as officials lament 'abandoned crisis' 15/04/2026 US blockade of Iranian ports 'fully implemented' 15/04/2026 Live: Reports of possible Israel-Lebanon ceasefire 15/04/2026 'War on women and girls' : Sexual violence the 'blueprint and strategy' of Sudan's brutal civil war 15/04/2026 Africa Kanye West Marseille concert postponed after anti-Semitic remarks 15/04/2026 168 children killed by Israel's strikes in Lebanon 15/04/2026 Israel-Lebanon talks: US Rubio hails 'historic opportunity' even amid challenges 15/04/2026 Pope heads to Cameroon with message of peace for conflict zone 15/04/2026"
